    "ledger": [
      {
        "id": "E1",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "LLMON: An LLM-Native Markup Language, now in Granite 4.1 3B and 8B",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/ibm-granite/llmon-an-llm-native-markup-language-now-in-granite",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-12T19:07:35.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-13T17:42:50.392Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E2",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "To address this, we developed LLMON (LLM Object Notation, pronounced “lemon”), an LLM-native markup language for explicitly communicating structure and semantics to the models.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/ibm-granite/llmon-an-llm-native-markup-language-now-in-granite",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-12T19:07:35.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-13T17:42:50.392Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E3",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Today we are releasing two experimental preview models, derived from Granite 4.1 base models, trained to consume and generate LLMON-marked text: granite-4.1-3b-LLMON-preview and granite-4.1-8b-LLMON-preview .",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/ibm-granite/llmon-an-llm-native-markup-language-now-in-granite",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-12T19:07:35.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-13T17:42:50.392Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E4",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "This is achieved while maintaining general capability relative to Granite 4.1 Instruct models.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/ibm-granite/llmon-an-llm-native-markup-language-now-in-granite",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-12T19:07:35.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-13T17:42:50.392Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E5",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "The LLMON preview models ship with their own chat template, so you build the same messages list you would pass to any chat model and call apply_chat_template as usual; it renders the LLMON shown below.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/ibm-granite/llmon-an-llm-native-markup-language-now-in-granite",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-12T19:07:35.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-13T17:42:50.392Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "LLMON practically eliminates the problem on this benchmark, avoiding 47% more attacks relative to the best frontier model that we tested, and 95% more than the best open-source model.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/ibm-granite/llmon-an-llm-native-markup-language-now-in-granite",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-12T19:07:35.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-13T17:42:50.392Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Across standard benchmark categories, the LLMON models perform on par with the Granite 4.1 Instruct models.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/ibm-granite/llmon-an-llm-native-markup-language-now-in-granite",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-12T19:07:35.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-13T17:42:50.392Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "In short, if you’re experimenting with Granite 4.1 3B or 8B today, you can swap in the LLMON preview and should see comparable general performance with much stronger resistance to prompt injection.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/ibm-granite/llmon-an-llm-native-markup-language-now-in-granite",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-12T19:07:35.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-13T17:42:50.392Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E9",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "The models start from Granite 4.1 base checkpoints rather than the released instruct models, so LLMON behavior is learned during post-training rather than layered on an existing chat format.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/ibm-granite/llmon-an-llm-native-markup-language-now-in-granite",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-12T19:07:35.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-13T17:42:50.392Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E10",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Models: granite-4.1-3b-LLMON-preview & granite-4.1-8b-LLMON-preview",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/ibm-granite/llmon-an-llm-native-markup-language-now-in-granite",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-12T19:07:35.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-13T17:42:50.392Z"
      },
